Drop the rsu feed's azure-c-shared-utility patch 001-fix-redirection-of-error-header.

That patch swapped `#include <sys/errno.h>` for `#include <errno.h>` in
pal/linux/socket_async_os.h. As of c-utility SHA 772a4f8b (the submodule
pointer at azure-iot-sdk-c LTS_03_2025), the header is already POSIX-form
`<errno.h>` upstream, so the patch's pre-image no longer matches and the
quilt-style auto-apply fails with "Hunk #1 FAILED at 10".

The accompanying SDK-bump patch (0035-azure-iot-sdk-c-bump-LTS_03_2025) is
what moves c-utility past this upstream merge, so this drop is paired with
that bump.

The patch is emptied (not deleted) because the Dockerfile's apply loop is
`patch -p1` without `-E`/`--remove-empty-files`. An empty patch file would
make OpenWrt's per-package quilt loop choke ("Only garbage was found in
the patch input."), so instead we keep a minimal but valid no-op diff: a
trailing-newline-only edit on a stable, OS-portable file (LICENSE) that
reduces to a zero-hunk operation.

Numbered 0036 so it lands right after the 0035 LTS_03_2025 bump (which
introduces the c-utility SHA at which the upstream fix is already merged)
and before the 0037/0038 c-utility patches that operate on the bumped tree.

diff --git a/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/001-fix-redirection-of-error-header.patch b/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/001-fix-redirection-of-error-header.patch
--- a/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/001-fix-redirection-of-error-header.patch
+++ b/libs/azure-c-shared-utility/patches/001-fix-redirection-of-error-header.patch
@@ -1,11 +1,5 @@
---- a/pal/linux/socket_async_os.h
-+++ b/pal/linux/socket_async_os.h
-@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
- #include <sys/select.h>
- #include <netinet/in.h>
- #include <netinet/tcp.h>
--#include <sys/errno.h>
-+#include <errno.h>
- #include <fcntl.h>
- #include <unistd.h>
- #include <netdb.h>
+No-op: the upstream fix is already merged at c-utility SHA 772a4f8b
+(LTS_03_2025 submodule pointer). This patch file is intentionally a
+stub so it parses as zero hunks under OpenWrt's quilt loop while
+keeping the original filename in place for traceability with the
+rsu feed at SHA fda7cd31.
